  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197448",
      "title": "Using the React DevTools",
      "lectureOrder": 43,
      "videoOrder": 40,
      "sourceHash": "453957e23ca903f8b21ba0224555c5621b4811b0d0ac3ec45ea6b95849490d76",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "Now Remote Debugging can be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 6.28,
          "en": "for certain situations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.28,
          "end": 9.66,
          "en": "What I personally find more useful is to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.66,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "the React developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 14.83,
          "en": "and not some specific React native developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.83,
          "end": 18.12,
          "en": "but the regular React devtools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.12,
          "end": 20.98,
          "en": "Now you might know the React devtools as an extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.98,
          "end": 22.87,
          "en": "you can install in your browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.87,
          "end": 26.72,
          "en": "and that extension will not work for React native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.72,
          "end": 30.07,
          "en": "But what you can do here in a separate terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.07,
          "end": 33.5,
          "en": "is you can install them globally on your system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.5,
          "end": 35.96,
          "en": "or also as a project only dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.96,
          "end": 37.9,
          "en": "but here I'll install them globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.9,
          "end": 41.52,
          "en": "with npm install -g react -devtools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 44.6,
          "en": "and here on MacOS, I need to add a sudo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.6,
          "end": 46.18,
          "en": "in front of this to make it work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.18,
          "end": 48.88,
          "en": "You might not need to do that on windows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.88,
          "end": 49.96,
          "en": "You definitely don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.96,
          "end": 54.31,
          "en": "because sudo doesn't exist there and isn't required there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.31,
          "end": 57.8,
          "en": "And if you hit enter and you install this package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.8,
          "end": 60.1,
          "en": "what this will give you is a standalone version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.1,
          "end": 61.773,
          "en": "of the React devtools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.42,
          "end": 65.08,
          "en": "With the devtools installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.08,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "you can start and by running react -devtools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "like this as a standalone command in the terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "And please note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 76.43299999999999,
          "en": "that I still have my npm start process up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.32,
          "end": 79.91,
          "en": "And this opens up a new window.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.91,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "This opens up this devtools window here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 85.59,
          "en": "Now with that up and running, you can go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.59,
          "end": 90.59,
          "en": "to your simulator, to your app and open that builtin menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.68,
          "end": 97.68,
          "en": "that development menu and enable Debug Remote JS again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.85,
          "end": 100.67,
          "en": "And now the React devtool should connect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.67,
          "end": 104.53,
          "en": "Now you see that by the way, my color gets lost if I do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.53,
          "end": 106.07,
          "en": "seems to be a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.07,
          "end": 108.56,
          "en": "I don't know exactly where this is coming from here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.56,
          "end": 111.75999999999999,
          "en": "but the background color set in the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.75999999999999,
          "end": 113.67,
          "en": "Json file is getting lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.67,
          "end": 116.85,
          "en": "as I enable Remote JavaScript Debugging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 118.37,
          "en": "but it is what it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.37,
          "end": 122.44,
          "en": "Nonetheless now we got these React devtools up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.44,
          "end": 125.07,
          "en": "and in those tools, that's the nice thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 128.04,
          "en": "You can see your component tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 129.49,
          "en": "You can see the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.49,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "you see all these devtools components like view and button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "and then the components that are part of the builtin button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "which can also be interesting to look into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "you see your goal input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 142.61,
          "en": "And what's really nice is if you click on a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.61,
          "end": 146.39,
          "en": "you see the props it gets and the values of those props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.39,
          "end": 149.07999999999998,
          "en": "and you see any state you have in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.07999999999998,
          "end": 151.963,
          "en": "And as I, for example, start typing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.16,
          "end": 155.69,
          "en": "You see that this state updates here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.69,
          "end": 157.64,
          "en": "and you can even change this state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.64,
          "end": 161.77,
          "en": "to simulate different things and to test different things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.77,
          "end": 164.77,
          "en": "And you see this updated state gets reflected back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.77,
          "end": 165.993,
          "en": "into the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.92000000000002,
          "end": 170.47,
          "en": "And these React devtools are really nice to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.47,
          "end": 173.66,
          "en": "because being able to look into your component tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.66,
          "end": 175.67000000000002,
          "en": "whilst your app is running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.67000000000002,
          "end": 178.48,
          "en": "and analyzing your state and your props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.48,
          "end": 182.03,
          "en": "and even changing those values can be super useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.03,
          "end": 184.713,
          "en": "especially as you're building more complex apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.59,
          "end": 187.57,
          "en": "Now, of course, if you don't need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.57,
          "end": 190.12,
          "en": "you might want to not run this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.12,
          "end": 193.76,
          "en": "and you might want to actually disable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.76,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "this Remote Debugging in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 198.38,
          "en": "since it can cause some performance issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.38,
          "end": 201.85,
          "en": "but it is a nice to have feature here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.85,
          "end": 205.203,
          "en": "Now with that, I will reload though and get rid of this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
